<section class="section" id="security">
  <div class="container security__grid">
    <div class="security__copy" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Private by construction</p>
      <h2 class="h2">
        Trust is checked,<br />
        <span class="h2--muted">never assumed.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Every control channel is paired explicitly and encrypted end to end. The
        optional rendezvous relay routes metadata only — it can never read your
        payloads.
      </p>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
            <path d="M8.5 12.5l2.5 2.5 4.5-5.5" />
          </svg>
          SHA-256 verification codes approved on both devices before first contact
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
            <path d="M8.5 12.5l2.5 2.5 4.5-5.5" />
          </svg>
          X25519 key agreement with forward-secret, per-session keys
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
            <path d="M8.5 12.5l2.5 2.5 4.5-5.5" />
          </svg>
          ChaCha20-Poly1305 on every packet, with monotonic replay windows
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
            <path d="M8.5 12.5l2.5 2.5 4.5-5.5" />
          </svg>
          Identity keys live in the Keychain, this device only — never synced
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="pair-card d-2" data-reveal>
      <p class="pair-card__head">
        <span class="pair-card__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        FrameLink · paired
      </p>
      <p class="pair-card__code">417&nbsp;<span>823</span></p>
      <div class="pair-card__divider" role="presentation"></div>
      <p class="pair-card__caption">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M12 3l7 2.8v5.4c0 4.4-3 8-7 9.8-4-1.8-7-5.4-7-9.8V5.8L12 3Z" />
          <path d="M9 12l2.2 2.2L15.4 10" />
        </svg>
        The same verification code appears on both devices. Nothing pairs until
        you compare and approve it — a nearby name is never a credential.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
